  "notes": "The same entity as Home Assistant 2026.10.4 sends it with unit_system us_customary: tomorrowio.json's values fed to Home Assistant's WeatherEntity as native values in the units its attributes state (°C, hPa, km/h, km, mm), state and forecasts read back through the weather component with hass.config.units set to US_CUSTOMARY_SYSTEM. Temperatures come back as whole °F (ints: outside °C the weather entity rounds to whole degrees), pressure in inHg, wind in mph, visibility in mi and precipitation in in, each to 2 decimals; humidity, bearings, conditions, datetimes and every other field are as in the metric file. The metric file's notes follow; their numbers are metric. State built from the test fixture's current values (tests/components/tomorrowio/fixtures/v4.json) run through weather.py. Forecasts are the snapshot's entries, with numbers re-converted below, from the 'Daily' entity (the only one new installs get; legacy ones may keep 'Hourly' and 'Nowcast' entities with the same forecasts). Current conditions carry ozone but never dew_point, apparent_temperature, wind_gust_speed, cloud_coverage or uv_index; each is present only when the API gives it. Forecasts carry humidity and dew_point only when the API gives them (here only the first entry of each). Hourly datetimes fall at :48 past the hour; entries from before today (local) are dropped. At most 14 daily and 24 hourly entries. Daily precipitation is the average hourly intensity times 24. precipitation_probability is null when the API value isn't a number. Changes for realism (test-data artefacts): core's fixture holds imperial numbers (F, inHg, mph, mi, in/h) that the test reads as metric, giving 44.1 C and 30.35 hPa. Every number here is the fixture's raw value fed to Home Assistant 2026.10.4's weather entity as °F/inHg/mph/mi/in and converted to the metric units the attributes claim (now 44.1 -> 6.7 C, 30.35 -> 1027.77 hPa, 33.59 -> 15.02 km/h, 8.15 -> 13.12 km). now was the test's frozen clock, 2021-03-06T23:59:59+00:00, 18 hours before the data begins; it is now 2021-03-07T17:48:00+00:00, the time of the fixture's readings, which are also its first hourly entry. The first hourly and first daily entries gave humidity 58 % beside a dew point of 12.76 F at 44.13 F, which means about 28 %; humidity is 28 % there (the current 23 % already agreed). The hour at 2021-03-08T03:48:00+00:00 has temperature -0.0: Home Assistant rounds 31.91 F (-0.05 C) to one decimal and keeps the sign.",
